-- title:
--   Central–elliptic geometric side of a truncated twisted trace formula
-- statement:
--   Let $L/K$ be a finite Galois extension of number fields whose Galois group is generated by $\sigma$ (every $\tau$ lies in the subgroup of integral powers of $\sigma$), let $\alpha>0$ and $\beta$ be real, and let $\Phi_L\subseteq\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb A_L)$ lie in the slab $\{g:\|\det g\|\in[\alpha,\beta]\}$, where $\|\cdot\|$ is the module of the idele (the distributive Haar character), and be a fundamental domain for the image of $\mathrm{GL}_2(L)$ with respect to the adelic Haar measure of $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb A_L)$ restricted to that slab. Let $\nu_{Z_L}$ be a Haar measure on $(\mathbb A_L)^\times$ and $\Omega_L$ a fundamental domain for the image of $L^\times$; let $D$ be a descent datum, i.e. a homomorphism from $\mathrm{Gal}(L/K)$ to ring automorphisms of $\mathbb A_L$, continuous and compatible with $L\hookrightarrow\mathbb A_L$. Let $S_L$ be a finite set of primes of $\mathcal O_L$ containing every $w$ with ramification index over $\mathcal O_K$ different from $1$, and $\xi_L$ a homomorphism from the full unit group of $\mathbb A_L$ to $\mathbb C^\times$, continuous as a complex-valued function and trivial on $L^\times$. Let $S$ be a finite set of primes of $\mathcal O_K$, $\varphi_a$ a function on $\mathrm{GL}_2$ of the infinite adeles of $L$ and $\varphi_S$ a family of functions on $\mathrm{GL}_2(L\otimes_K K_v)$; let $c>0$ and $u,d_1,d_2$ be real, $T_c\subseteq\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb A_L)$ compact, and $\Phi_0$ a further fundamental domain inside the same slab, contained in the union over $y\in T_c$ of the right translates by $y$ of the centre-cut Siegel set with parameters $c,u,d_1,d_2$ (integral finite part, local height at least $c$ at each infinite place, window quantity at most $u^2$, archimedean determinant norms in $[d_1,d_2]$). The assertion is that for every finite set $T$ of primes of $\mathcal O_K$ disjoint from $S$ with at least two elements and with no prime of $L$ above $T$ in $S_L$, every choice of a prime $w_v$ of $L$ above each $v$, of primes $w'_v$ with $(w'_v)$ the ideal $\sigma\cdot(w_v)$ for $v\in T$, of elements $\varpi_v$ of the valuation ring at $w_v$ that are irreducible and nonzero in $L_{w_v}$ for $v\in T$, of integers $n_v$ and families $r_v:\mathrm{Fin}\,n_v\to\mathrm{GL}_2(L_{w_v})$ which for $v\in T$ form a Hecke coset system for the integral subgroup $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathcal O_{w_v})$ and $\mathrm{diag}(\varpi_v,1)$ (representatives lying in the double coset, covering it modulo the integral subgroup, with injective images in the quotient), and of elements $z_v$ equal to the scalar matrix $\varpi_v\cdot 1$ for $v\in T$, there exist $\mu,\nu$ assigning to each pair $(ks,js)$ of functions from primes of $\mathcal O_K$ to $\mathbb N$ a complex number, such that for some constant $C$ one has $\|\mu\,ks\,js\|+\|\nu\,ks\,js\|\le C\prod_{v\in T}\bigl((N(w'_v)+1)\sqrt{|\xi_L(\det h_{w'_v})|}\bigr)^{ks\,v}\,|\xi_L(\det h_{w'_v})|^{js\,v}$, where $h_{w'_v}$ is the Hecke generator at $w'_v$, and such that for all $ks,js$ and all $\varphi$ on $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb A_L)$ and $\varphi_f$ on $\mathrm{GL}_2$ of the finite adeles constituting a semi-local factorisation relative to $S\cup T$ with archimedean factor $\varphi_a$, finite factor $\varphi_f$, and local factor at $v\in T$ given by $x\mapsto\sum_{\iota:\mathrm{Fin}(ks\,v)\to\mathrm{Fin}(n_v)}\mathbf 1_{\text{semi-local integral set}}\bigl(g_{\iota}^{-1}x\bigr)$ with $g_\iota$ the semi-local component of the local embedding of $\bigl(\prod_m r_v(\iota\,m)\bigr)z_v^{js\,v}$, and by $\varphi_S\,v$ off $T$, there is $R_0$ with the following property for all $R\ge R_0$: the integral over $x\in\Phi_0$ and $z\in\Omega_L$ of $\xi_L(z)$ times the value at $z\cdot x$ of the truncation at level $\exp R$ of the $\sigma$-twisted kernel $y\mapsto\sum^{\mathrm f}_{\gamma\in\mathrm{GL}_2(L)}\varphi(x^{-1}\gamma\,D(\sigma)(y))$, that is, of that kernel minus, on the set where the adelic height exceeds $\exp R$, its constant term along the unipotent $t\mapsto\begin{pmatrix}1&t\\0&1\end{pmatrix}$ with respect to additive adelic Haar measure conditioned on the adelic box, equals the integral over $x\in\Phi_L$ and $z\in\Omega_L$ of $\xi_L(z)$ times $\sum^{\mathrm f}_{\delta}\varphi\bigl(x^{-1}\delta\,D(\sigma)(z\cdot x)\bigr)$, the finite-support sum running over those $\delta\in\mathrm{GL}_2(L)$ whose $\sigma$-twisted conjugacy class has twisted norm class equal to the conjugacy class of some $\gamma\in\mathrm{GL}_2(K)$ that is either elliptic (its characteristic polynomial has no root in $K$) or central (a scalar matrix), plus $R\cdot(\nu\,ks\,js)+\mu\,ks\,js$.
--
--   This is the geometric side of the $\sigma$-twisted trace formula for $\mathrm{GL}_2$ over a cyclic extension $L/K$, computed along words in the Hecke operators at two or more unramified shift places: after truncation at height $\exp R$ the twisted kernel integral reduces to the central and elliptic twisted classes, up to a remainder that is affine in $R$ with coefficients bounded in terms of the Hecke word. It feeds the atomic form of this identity used to compare the twisted cut trace with its symmetric counterpart.
